---
<section id="fit-guide" class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-display-lg mb-4">Fit Diagnostic</h2>
    <p class="text-body-lg text-body max-w-2xl">A calculated size is a starting point. Your bra should fit perfectly without digging or slipping. Diagnose fit issues below.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    <details class="group bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-md p-6 cursor-pointer">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-medium text-body-md-strong list-none">
        The band is riding up my back
        <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 text-body text-body-sm pt-4 border-t border-hairline">
        <p>If the band rides up, it is too loose. The band should sit perfectly level around your ribcage. <strong>Fix:</strong> Try a tighter sister size (e.g., if you wear 36C, try 34D).</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-md p-6 cursor-pointer">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-medium text-body-md-strong list-none">
        My straps keep falling off
        <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 text-body text-body-sm pt-4 border-t border-hairline">
        <p>This often happens when the band is too loose, causing the straps to sit too far apart on your shoulders. <strong>Fix:</strong> First, tighten the straps. If that fails, go down a band size and up a cup size.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-md p-6 cursor-pointer">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-medium text-body-md-strong list-none">
        My breasts are bulging out (spillage)
        <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 text-body text-body-sm pt-4 border-t border-hairline">
        <p>If there is a "double-boob" effect or spillage at the top or sides, the cup is too small. <strong>Fix:</strong> Keep your band size the same, but increase the cup size (e.g., 34B to 34C).</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-md p-6 cursor-pointer">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-medium text-body-md-strong list-none">
        There are gaps in the cups
        <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 text-body text-body-sm pt-4 border-t border-hairline">
        <p>If there is space between your breast and the cup, the cup is too large or the style doesn't suit your breast shape. <strong>Fix:</strong> Try going down a cup size (e.g., 34D to 34C).</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  details > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
